                <div class="azure-notes-content">
                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">For Flexible Server Deployment:

There are 2 primary modes of design:

    •   Zone Redundant Architecture: This design will create a primary database server in the
        availability zone (like east us). Another server with the exact same configurations will be
        placed in a different availability zone within the same region (like east us 2). This model
        provides higher fault tolerance, but higher latency in transmitting traffic.
    •   Same Zone Architecture: In this design, both your primary and secondary servers are placed
        within the same availability zone. Data transmission is faster, latency is lower due to the
        servers being physically close. However, fault tolerance is lower.

    •   With both architectures, users can provision read replicas for backup and database
        consistency. Read replicas is a read-only copy of your Azure database, designed to reduce the
        load on your primary server.</pre>
                    <div class="text-center my-4">
                        <img src="/Images/AzureNotes/Chapter_8_-_Microsoft_Azure_-_Database_Availability_and_Consistency_For_Azure_SQL/p02-000.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-sm" alt="For Flexible Server Deployment: - source image" />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    

